{"title":"2026 BmMT Individual Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"border: 1px solid #444; background: #fff; max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto 20px auto; font-size: 90%; line-height: 1.6; font-family: sans-serif;\">\n<div style=\"background: #e0dbff; padding: 12px; text-align: center; border-bottom: 1px solid #444;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 110%; font-weight: bold; color: #4b3ba7;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_(Answer_Key)\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual (Answer Key)\">2026 BmMT Individual (Answer Key)</a></span><br />\n<span style=\"font-size: 95%; color: #6c5cb8;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Berkeley_Mini_Math_Tournament&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Berkeley Mini Math Tournament (page does not exist)\">BmMT Resources</a> • <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Special:Upload&amp;wpDestFile=2026_BmMT_Individual.pdf\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual.pdf\">PDF</a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"padding: 15px 25px 15px 25px;\">\n<p style=\"font-weight: bold; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;\">Instructions</p>\n<ol style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 15px; padding-left: 20px;\">\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">This test contains 20 short answer questions. All answers must be expressed in simplest form unless specified otherwise. Only answers written inside the boxes on the answer sheet will be considered for grading.</li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">Each correct answer is worth 1 point. Each incorrect or blank answer is worth 0 points.</li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">No calculators are permitted. Protractors, rulers, and compasses are permitted.</li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">Figures are not necessarily drawn to scale.</li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">You will have <b>60 minutes</b> working time to complete the test.</li>\n</ol>\n<div style=\"text-align: center; border-top: 1px solid #eee; padding-top: 12px; font-weight: bold; word-spacing: 2px;\">\n<p><a href=\"#Problem_1\">1</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_2\">2</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_3\">3</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_4\">4</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_5\">5</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_6\">6</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_7\">7</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_8\">8</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_9\">9</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_10\">10</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_11\">11</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_12\">12</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_13\">13</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_14\">14</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_15\">15</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_16\">16</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_17\">17</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_18\">18</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_19\">19</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_20\">20</a>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Problem_16\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 16</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Problem_17\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 17</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Problem_18\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 18</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Problem_19\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">19</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 19</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Problem_20\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">20</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 20</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">21</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Hummus the cat has a black and white striped tail with 5 black segments and 6 white segments. Each black segment has length 1, and each white segment has length 1.5. How long is Hummus’s tail?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Isaac draws a circle with diameter 4. He then draws a new circle whose area is 4 times the area of the original circle. Compute the area of the new circle divided by the circumference of the new circle.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/4/a740ed697d1711a19ea04d9a2846614d141266f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\bar{\\wedge} b = 2a - b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"16\" />. Compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/c/a0c604524e8c0c32409b80c2559f028d0d84c337.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3 \\bar{\\wedge} 5) \\bar{\\wedge} 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Aarush writes the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> on a whiteboard. Every minute, he replaces the current number on the whiteboard, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/5/0a5dcc157a1564c55ef9cb3c70f05b8473bf1a09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 - n$\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />. What number is written on the board after 2026 minutes?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many ways are there to order the letters in “BMMT” such that the two M’s are next to each other? For example, two such orderings are “BMMT” and “TMMB.”\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Four congruent rectangles are arranged to form a large outer square with a small square hole in the center. The side length of the large outer square is 14, and the side length of the small square hole is 2. What is the length of the diagonal of one of the four rectangles?\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:Missing_Diagram&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:Missing Diagram (page does not exist)\">Template:Missing Diagram</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Jonathan and Mary go out to eat. Jonathan always tips 15% of his bill, and Mary always tips 25% of hers. If Jonathan orders spaghetti and Mary orders risotto, they pay exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/2/d0251739a96cd868c9aa116b3cbe2b2711a2e8bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$55.50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> (including tips) in total. If instead Jonathan orders risotto and Mary orders spaghetti, they pay exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/f/5dfda16822c5f9f2c8f091acb451eecbbfab4286.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$54.90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> (including tips) in total. What is the sum of the costs of spaghetti and risotto without tipping?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Compute the sum of all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/3/7b37a9925d526887d132907a4a7b052a03023920.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4(x + 11)^2 = 9(x + 1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"180\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Compute the smallest positive whole number with the property that the product of its digits is 120.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Kaity is moving several boxes from her van to the classroom. She picks up either one or two boxes at the van, carries them to the classroom, drops off the boxes, and then walks back to the van, repeating the process until all the boxes are in the classroom and she is back at the van. Her walking speed when carrying no boxes is 2.8 miles per hour, and her walking speed when carrying one box is 2.4 miles per hour. She finds that it doesn’t matter whether she carries one box or two boxes at a time: either way, it will take the same amount of time to move all of the boxes. What is Kaity’s walking speed in miles per hour while carrying two boxes? Assume that Kaity picks up and drops off the boxes immediately.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define the drift of a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/f/adfd9ae8a3fac031d3b8b470a52a709a23d4d6d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> in the coordinate plane as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/5/a859acebdd07c34704648be45c0daf108e2a29d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />. Three corners of a square in the coordinate plane have drifts of 8, 11, and 25, in some order. What is the maximum possible drift of the fourth corner of the square?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 11\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Ben and Theo enter a classroom with the number 0 written on the blackboard. Ben and Theo repeatedly take turns replacing the number on the blackboard, with Ben going first. Ben writes the smallest multiple of 3 greater than the current number and Theo writes the smallest multiple of 4 greater than the current number. The first few numbers that appear on the blackboard are 0, 3, 4, 6, 8, ... . What is the 100th number that appears on the blackboard, including the initial 0?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 12 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For each positive whole number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/1/701599597b8c249dcfb73949fb3de09acbde7ac0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T(n) = 1 + 2 + 3 + \\dots + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"213\" height=\"20\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />th triangular number. It is known that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/1/5b1792b84f3a3ca37dbc2de5f917a0bb4b0ae119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T(n) = n(n+ 1)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"20\" />. What is the sum of all positive whole numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/0/5b0587b82f0e10f15562839ea5c19e5ad1d5de10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{T(m + 2) + T(m + 4)}{T(m)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"177\" height=\"45\" /> is a whole number?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 13 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Jessica has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/3/a832b76c4f4a4ec13ac1b557da4fed6006e64d00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> grid of square cells. In how many ways can she color two cells red and the remaining four cells blue if colorings that differ by a rotation are considered the same, but colorings that differ by a reflection are considered different?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/d/62d4eeb6a966219df4ac79cfc9981ec095e6be0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> Sudoku solution, each column, row, and bolded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4c044326e2e84b768dafef07060bd42b0a5cb21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> region contains exactly one of each digit from 1 to 4, and each cell contains exactly one digit. A Sudoku solution is <i>super</i> if each of the two main diagonals also contains exactly one of each digit from 1 to 4. How many distinct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/d/62d4eeb6a966219df4ac79cfc9981ec095e6be0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> super Sudoku solutions exist if rotations and reflections are considered distinct?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 15 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_16\">Problem 16</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 16\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An ordered triple of numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/0/d80414f2f94f70731e91b6e12c4e6934c8fa65de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b, c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> is stable if it is equal to a permutation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/4/b84e60f71d0f875062ead76058fecfd66682f3e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(|a-b|, |b-c|, |c-a|)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"180\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/4/2e4b746328d0cbf6006be8ea2ffa2837b0cd4210.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c \\le 2026$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"132\" height=\"17\" />. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d4e5fa16269a1c2026a4a1a9e79fc512b921dd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/b/40b96e517f0ec85ef5a098d172c78238ca062e32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 1, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" /> are stable. Compute the number of stable ordered triples of nonnegative integers.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 16 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_17\">Problem 17</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 17\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/7/fb71d5ba363a314c0343efdd9a19aafe8070c75e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = BC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" /> and is inscribed in circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> passes through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and intersects line segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/7908ad0f396f05f3de405cf8f7f68d0db3ff8a7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D \\ne A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" />. Line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/f/3ff9d2add1273f7f294d4f0318b0ed4340c07768.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> passes through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and is parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/970a3f7a0a3b548d0684d391994a6366f8d71ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> is tangent to circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/f/3ff9d2add1273f7f294d4f0318b0ed4340c07768.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" />, intersecting it at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/c/c3ce151b3a820d2d1ba3e948e7a79ac0a698c13e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EC = \\frac{16}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"38\" /> and that the longest side length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is 16, compute the radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> divided by the radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 17 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_18\">Problem 18</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 18\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A permutation of the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/0/af04b55f63d2d95f7ea06b488925b6a9a98a28dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, \\dots, 10\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" /> is called <i>mountainous</i> if the elements increase to a peak and then decrease. The peak cannot be the first or the last element. What fraction of mountainous permutations have the property that the sum of the first element and the last element is odd?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 18 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_19\">Problem 19</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 19\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be distinct real numbers. The parabolas <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/c/4ec86c76ed3e655d17ffc88954043e062826de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 2026x^2 + cx + d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba46fa7a062d3f47f97ae3f3b1c166bb5664712.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = -2026x^2 + dx + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"176\" height=\"20\" /> are graphed in the coordinate plane. There are two lines that are tangent to both parabolas, and their slopes are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2c760e4463aebecbb3ad5c92c623f2c71656c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c - d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 19\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_20\">Problem 20</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 20\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/6521ad84932f05bbfa1185b24d793813c7aefc2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, C, D,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"85\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie on a circle in that order such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/f/2bfaa86e188b815f259ec79ec03d68d9808387a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABD = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/6/e06b52410f4d0f0c89d0e08a5ba39c4cdb6dcdbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADC = \\angle CBE = 60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"189\" height=\"15\" />. Segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c970cbf5e2e7029089517d5e8efbb8cade6d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> intersect at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. The circle passing through points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/f/ccf6d387ce491c0ca100c134021f21f616d75162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/c/4ec42d731653ed6bea8a4c5f8cdd4a1de45a8bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G \\ne A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />. Given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/5/855f3b2a26f0b3cdee3caac7796c109dd88a83a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/0/c102879f85158a055d59dfeb580d085ead9292f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DF = 8$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11fca7fa0396390456782405b2897976a413f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 20 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=21\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:BmMT_Individual_box&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:BmMT Individual box (page does not exist)\">Template:BmMT Individual box</a>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Berkeley_Mini_Math_Tour